{
  "recordedOn": "2026-10-31",
  "author": "Smoebo",
  "branch": "grok/enemy-npc-race-matrix",
  "approval": "Approved by Albert (@Smoebo) on 2026-10-31, including the canted longbow draw; no vote record was supplied.",
  "source": "Painted outside the repository's ComfyUI job list and shipped as 256x256 WebP. The generation tool, prompts and original images were not supplied with the art; the scripts/placeholder-set.mjs ENEMY_NPC_VARIANT entries describe each subject for the silhouette generator and are not the prompts these paintings came from.",
  "missing": [
    "generation prompts",
    "original image hashes",
    "encoding settings"
  ],
  "subjectBasis": "Original designs of generic SRD 5.1 humanoid foes (bandit, cultist, scout as archer, knight as dark knight) in the four most common SRD races (human, elf, dwarf, half-orc). No subject is on the creature-art watch list.",
  "designNotes": [
    "Poses are aggressive: these NPCs are usually the enemy.",
    "Dwarf archers carry crossbows (the dwarven crossbow trope); the human, elf and half-orc archers draw a longbow at a canted near-vertical angle rather than the horizontal draw films and games popularised.",
    "Every dark knight wears one locked design: an open-faced horned helm with cheek guards, sword raised.",
    "Only the common races are covered by design. A rare race (a drow) would get at most one face later, and until then draws its character-race portrait."
  ],
  "review": "Every plate inspected at full size and in a round crop at 96px and 40px on dark and light surrounds, 2026-10-31. Previews: enemy-npc-race-matrix-2026-10-31.webp.",
  "addedBytes": 493498,
